From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kuniyuki Iwashima <kuniyu@amazon.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Apr 2025 17:03:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ipv6: Get rid of RTNL for SIOCADDRT and RTM_NEWROUTE.

Link: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/169fd62799e8acabbfb4760799be11138ced949c

Now we are ready to remove RTNL from SIOCADDRT and RTM_NEWROUTE.

The remaining things to do are

  1. pass false to lwtunnel_valid_encap_type_attr()
  2. use rcu_dereference_rtnl() in fib6_check_nexthop()
  3. place rcu_read_lock() before ip6_route_info_create_nh().

Let's complete the RTNL-free conversion.

When each CPU-X adds 100000 routes on table-X in a batch
concurrently on c7a.metal-48xl EC2 instance with 192 CPUs,

without this series:

  $ sudo ./route_test.sh
  ...
  added 19200000 routes (100000 routes * 192 tables).
  time elapsed: 191577 milliseconds.

with this series:

  $ sudo ./route_test.sh
  ...
  added 19200000 routes (100000 routes * 192 tables).
  time elapsed: 62854 milliseconds.

I changed the number of routes in each table (1000 ~ 100000)
and consistently saw it finish 3x faster with this series.

Note that now every caller of lwtunnel_valid_encap_type() passes
false as the last argument, and this can be removed later.

Signed-off-by: Kuniyuki Iwashima <kuniyu@amazon.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20250418000443.43734-16-kuniyu@amazon.com
Signed-off-by: Paolo Abeni <pabeni@redhat.com>

Backport to Azure Linux 6.6.161.1: Use the 6.6 rtnl_register_module() API.
Keep IPv6 deletion handlers and SIOCDELRT under RTNL; only
NEWROUTE/SIOCADDRT are unlocked. Pass the corresponding lock state to
tunnel validation. The RCU lifetime fix 8e5f1bb81274 is applied first, so
omit the broad RCU sections it removes and avoid importing transient
allocation changes.

Signed-off-by: Alex Cortelyou <alcortel@microsoft.com>
---
 net/ipv4/nexthop.c |  4 ++--
 net/ipv6/route.c   | 11 ++++++-----
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/ipv4/nexthop.c b/net/ipv4/nexthop.c
index 9a503bf..6779cff 100644
--- a/net/ipv4/nexthop.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/nexthop.c
@@ -1315,12 +1315,12 @@ int fib6_check_nexthop(struct nexthop *nh, struct fib6_config *cfg,
 	if (nh->is_group) {
 		struct nh_group *nhg;
 
-		nhg = rtnl_dereference(nh->nh_grp);
+		nhg = rcu_dereference_rtnl(nh->nh_grp);
 		if (nhg->has_v4)
 			goto no_v4_nh;
 		is_fdb_nh = nhg->fdb_nh;
 	} else {
-		nhi = rtnl_dereference(nh->nh_info);
+		nhi = rcu_dereference_rtnl(nh->nh_info);
 		if (nhi->family == AF_INET)
 			goto no_v4_nh;
 		is_fdb_nh = nhi->fdb_nh;
diff --git a/net/ipv6/route.c b/net/ipv6/route.c
index ae0ef2f..9e3af8f 100644
--- a/net/ipv6/route.c
+++ b/net/ipv6/route.c
@@ -4535,7 +4535,6 @@ int ipv6_route_ioctl(struct net *net, unsigned int cmd, struct in6_rtmsg *rtmsg)
 
 	rtmsg_to_fib6_config(net, rtmsg, &cfg);
 
-	rtnl_lock();
 	switch (cmd) {
 	case SIOCADDRT:
 		/* Only do the default setting of fc_metric in route adding */
@@ -4544,10 +4543,11 @@ int ipv6_route_ioctl(struct net *net, unsigned int cmd, struct in6_rtmsg *rtmsg)
 		err = ip6_route_add(&cfg, GFP_KERNEL, NULL);
 		break;
 	case SIOCDELRT:
+		rtnl_lock();
 		err = ip6_route_del(&cfg, NULL);
+		rtnl_unlock();
 		break;
 	}
-	rtnl_unlock();
 	return err;
 }
 
@@ -5077,6 +5077,7 @@ static int rtm_to_fib6_config(struct sk_buff *skb, struct nlmsghdr *nlh,
 			      struct fib6_config *cfg,
 			      struct netlink_ext_ack *extack)
 {
+	bool newroute = nlh->nlmsg_type == RTM_NEWROUTE;
 	struct rtmsg *rtm;
 	struct nlattr *tb[RTA_MAX+1];
 	unsigned int pref;
@@ -5183,7 +5184,7 @@ static int rtm_to_fib6_config(struct sk_buff *skb, struct nlmsghdr *nlh,
 
 		err = lwtunnel_valid_encap_type_attr(cfg->fc_mp,
 						     cfg->fc_mp_len,
-						     extack, true);
+						     extack, !newroute);
 		if (err < 0)
 			goto errout;
 	}
@@ -5203,7 +5204,7 @@ static int rtm_to_fib6_config(struct sk_buff *skb, struct nlmsghdr *nlh,
 		cfg->fc_encap_type = nla_get_u16(tb[RTA_ENCAP_TYPE]);
 
 		err = lwtunnel_valid_encap_type(cfg->fc_encap_type,
-						extack, true);
+						extack, !newroute);
 		if (err < 0)
 			goto errout;
 	}
@@ -6838,7 +6839,7 @@ int __init ip6_route_init(void)
 		goto fib6_rules_init;
 
 	ret = rtnl_register_module(THIS_MODULE, PF_INET6, RTM_NEWROUTE,
-				   inet6_rtm_newroute, NULL, 0);
+				   inet6_rtm_newroute, NULL, RTNL_FLAG_DOIT_UNLOCKED);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		goto out_register_late_subsys;
 
